course: dictionary
lesson: 5768
title: A grand word for lunch
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words are fancy versions of ordinary words. «A luncheon will be served» sounds grander than «lunch will be served», and both mean a meal at midday. Luncheon means a lunch, often a formal one for a group or a special event. The words around it give you clues.
explain: Look at this: «Trot up and down the towing-path as hard as you can, till you're warm and dry again, while I dive for the luncheon-basket.» You dive for things, and a basket is for carrying things. A luncheon-basket must hold food, so a luncheon is a meal you pack and carry. Swap in your meaning and check it still fits.
explain: Now «He orders the best luncheon that could be provided at so short a notice.» The hotel must make a special meal quickly, so luncheon here means a posh, formal lunch. In everyday talk, though, you would just say lunch.
fact: Luncheon means a lunch, especially a formal one for a group or special event.
fact: Luncheon is mostly found in formal invitations and old stories; in everyday talk, say «lunch».
fact: Luncheon meat is cooked, pressed meat sold in tins or slices, often called Spam.
fact: Phrases you may see include luncheon party, charity luncheon and luncheon voucher.
fact: «Incautiously» means carelessly, so the Rat was careless when he let slip that the Mole and the Badger would be out till luncheon time.
exercise: «A luncheon will be served at the town hall for the new hospital.» What is a luncheon here? | *A formal lunch for a group | A long walk along a river | A bedtime story | A tin of cooked meat
exercise: «...while I dive for the luncheon-basket.» What is a luncheon-basket most likely for? | Keeping the boat dry | *Carrying food for a meal | Catching fish from the river | Carrying water to the horses
exercise: Ella says luncheon is just a fancy word. What is the best everyday word to say instead? | Supper | Breakfast | *Lunch | Teatime
test: «He orders the best luncheon that could be provided at so short a notice.» What does this tell you about the luncheon? | It was a cancelled meal that nobody ate | It was made by the children at home | It was a snack eaten in the rain | *It was a grand meal arranged quickly
test: What is luncheon meat? | A sandwich bread roll | *Cooked, pressed meat sold in tins or slices | A cold drink for summer | A cheese made in the hills
exam: Which sentence uses luncheon correctly? | Luncheon was the colour of the sky | *The mayor hosted a luncheon for the town's volunteers | The dog ate his luncheon and then went to bed | We went luncheon to the moon on Tuesday
